  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is consistently low (≤0.00) or negative, as models tend to overestimate prices in calm or bearish sentiment.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent 7-day true outcomes show strong mean reversion toward lower values after a spike.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent sentiment shifts — if sentiment rises above 0.33, adjust upward by 3-5% to reflect bullish momentum.",
    "Apply lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast 3-5 days prior, reduce current forecast by 5-8% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Cap forecast overshoots above +15% of recent 30-day average — especially after sentiment spikes — to prevent overreaction.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00–0.33) and true outcomes show persistent downward drift, apply a mild downward bias (−2–4%) to avoid overconfidence in short-term rebounds."
  ]
}
